      reveal_market: "There is no community market in Blackjack; the only shared information is the dealer's upcard.",
      buy_market: 'Players cannot purchase or swap cards from a market; new cards are obtained only via hitting.',
      buy_stock: "Cards are received from the dealer's shoe rather than being purchased from a stock pile.",
      fold: 'Once a bet is placed and cards are dealt, the player must play out the hand (or surrender if allowed).',
      check: 'Every hand requires a bet to be active; there is no checking mechanic in this banking game.',
      call: "Bets are made independently against the house rather than matching other players' wagers.",
      bet: 'Must be within table limits.',
      raise: 'Wagers are fixed after the deal, except for doubling down or splitting pairs.',
      declare: 'Hand strength is established during the showdown comparison rather than through a declaration.',
      reveal_hand: 'Hand reveal is managed automatically by the system logic during the settlement phase.',
      award_pot: 'Winning bets are paid directly by the house; there is no shared pot to award to a single winner.',
      play_card: 'Blackjack is a hand-value banking game where cards are held rather than played to a shared trick.',
      draw: 'Allowed only if current hand value is under 21.',
      discard: 'Players must keep all cards dealt to them; cards are only removed after the hand ends.',
      pass: 'May stand on any value.',
      bid: 'Blackjack uses a wagering system rather than an auction-style bidding system.',
